# Agent Workflow: Step-by-step execution with verification

For every non-trivial coding task in this repository, follow this workflow.

## Canonical project rules (do not duplicate)

Before changing code, read the relevant canonical docs:

- `docs/DOCS_CANONICAL_INDEX.md` (P0 overrules P1/P2)
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE_REFACTOR_CANONICAL.md` (P0 architecture boundaries)
- `docs/MODULE_INTEGRATION_POLICY.md` (P0 onboarding and integration rules)
- `docs/TEST_SMOKE_GATES.md` (P0 verification gates)

Architecture pointers (details live in the docs above):

- Fachliche business logic belongs in `modules/*` services only; `qm_platform/*` is platform/runtime infrastructure, not domain logic. Keep PyQt widgets and CLI parsers thin.
- External Python access to a module goes through `modules/<name>/api.py`; do not add new imports from module internals.
- Runtime ports, capabilities, settings contributions, and domain events are integration mechanisms, not alternative import surfaces.
- `src/backend/*` is a transport host; public backend imports go through `src/backend/api.py`.
- Verify features CLI-first before GUI integration.
- Before roadmap/backend/multiuser work, check `docs/MASTER_ORCHESTRATION_ROADMAP.md`.
- Do not combine multiple roadmap packages in one implementation task.

## Environment (this repo)

- OS/shell: Windows / PowerShell — chain commands with `;`, not `&&`.
- Python `3.14.x`; use the workspace venv explicitly:
  `$env:PYTHONPATH="."; .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest`.

## Workflow

1. Do not implement the whole task in one pass.
2. First create a short numbered plan with small, independently testable steps.
3. Execute exactly one step at a time.
4. After each step, run the smallest relevant verification command for the changed layer:

   | Change area | Command |
   | --- | --- |
| Platform/runtime | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/platform -q` |
| Module service/logic | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/modules -q` or targeted `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/modules/test_<module>_*.py -q` |
| PyQt/GUI adapter | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/interfaces -q` |
| CLI flow | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/e2e_cli -q` |
| Backend host | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m src.backend` and `GET /health` when the server is running |
| Runtime smoke | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m interfaces.cli.main health` |
| Stricter runtime check | `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m interfaces.cli.main doctor --strict` |

   This repo has no configured linter or typechecker (no ruff/flake8/mypy/pre-commit). Do not invent lint/typecheck steps.

5. Do not continue to the next implementation step if the previous step has failing tests, CLI smoke failures, or obvious regressions.
6. If a verification fails, fix the failure inside the current step before moving on.
7. After each step, report:
   - what changed
   - which files were touched
   - which verification command was run
   - whether it passed or failed
   - the next proposed step
8. For behavior changes, add or update tests before considering the step complete.
9. Before finalizing the task, run the broader relevant test suite unless it is clearly too expensive; if skipped, explain why. Use these broader gates when applicable:
   - full layer runs: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/platform -q`, `tests/modules -q`, `tests/interfaces -q`, `tests/e2e_cli -q`
   - packaging impact: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe packaging/build_onedir.py`
   - release/migration impact: `.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/golive_gate.py --output "<evidence-dir>/golive-gate.json"`
10. Prefer minimal, reviewable diffs over large rewrites.
